e study of inscription of ancient Assam and comparative literature as per the syllabus of Gauhati University.\nFaculty:\nAssociate Professor\nDr. Hari Prasad Baruah\nDr. Dalima Kakati\nAssistant Professor\nDr. Arindam kr. Deka\nAssistant Professor (T)\nPampy Barman\nSnigdha Sen\nAcademic Calendar (Session 2021-22) –\nDownload PDF\nProject\n: 01 (ICSSR Sponsored MRP)\nঅসমীয়া বিভাগ, Assamese Department\nEstd: 15-07-1970\nH.o.D: Dr. Hari Prasad Baruah\nDegree offered in: Assamese\nFaculty Strength: 6\nStudent Strength: 100\nDept. Library: Yes\nEx-Teachers\n:\nProf. Romala Bora\nProf. Jiban Ch. Kalita\nProf. Gauri Kanta Deka\nDr. Jogendra Saikia\nDr. Prabina Sarma\nPrograms, Courses & Facilities\nProgramme Offered:\nBA (Honours)\nBA (Regular)\nAdd on Course:\nAssamese Proofreading Skills\n1st Batch\nPhotograph\n1st Batch Student list\npdf\nFacilities\n:\nDepartment Library\nOne desktop (Computer) with Internet\nActivities\n:\nPublished annual Wall-magazine\nPublished departmental Bulletin\nOrganized Seminar/Popular Talk\nEducational Tour/Field study\nSociety\n:\nঅসমীয়া সাহিত্য চ’ৰা “Assamese Literary Society”\nWebinars Organized\n:\nOrganized National Webinar entitled “Assamese Language and Culture in the Perspective of Solar and Lunar Cult” held on 18th July 2020 Speaker: Prof. Amalendu Chakraborty, Vice-Chancellor, Rabindra Nath Thakur University, Assam.\nOrganized National Webinar entitled “Asamiya Bangla aru Udiya Bhsha : Parasparik Samparka Bichar” held on 6th August 2020 Speaker: Prof. Dipti Phukan Patgiri, Professor & Former Head, Department Of Assamese, Gauhati University, Assam.\nOrganized National Webinar entitled “Barnabaisamma aru Asamiya Samaj” held on 23rd July 2020 Speaker,: Mayur Borah, Distinguished Writer & Critic, Assam.\nTeaching Staff\nHari Prasad Baruah, Ph.D, M.Phil, M.A.\nH.o.D\nSpecialization\n:Language and Cultural Studies\nDOJ\n:02-05-2008\nEmail:\n:haripbaruah@gmail.com\nPhone:\n:9864201492\nView Profile\nDalima Kakati, Ph.D, M.Phil, M.A.\nAs